# CHECKS, never writes.
#
# This hook used to be `gjsify run format`, and it had no `git add`. So it
# rewrote the WORKING TREE while the commit captured the already-staged,
# unformatted content: it could not improve a single commit, and it left
# 120+ modified files behind every time. That is where the parked
# "formatter drift" stashes came from. A hook that writes what it cannot
# stage is pure loss.
#
# A check cannot do that. If this fails, run `gjsify run format`.
gjsify run check:format
